A. Commit message:
Fix potential null pointer dereference in xennet_close and xennet_destroy_queues

B. Change summary:
The changes ensure that the code checks for the existence of `info->queues` before accessing it, preventing a potential null pointer dereference. This fix is backported from a newer version to an older version.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/net/xen-netfront.c b/drivers/net/xen-netfront.c
--- a/drivers/net/xen-netfront.c
+++ b/drivers/net/xen-netfront.c
@@ -867,7 +867,7 @@ static int xennet_close(struct net_device *dev)
 {
 	struct netfront_info *np = netdev_priv(dev);
-	unsigned int num_queues = dev->real_num_tx_queues;
+	unsigned int num_queues = np->queues ? dev->real_num_tx_queues : 0;
 	unsigned int i;
 	struct netfront_queue *queue;
 	netif_tx_stop_all_queues(np->netdev);
@@ -881,6 +881,9 @@ static void xennet_destroy_queues(struct netfront_info *info)
 {
 	unsigned int i;
 
+	if (!info->queues)
+		return;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < info->netdev->real_num_tx_queues; i++) {
 		struct netfront_queue *queue = &info->queues[i];
```